---
import DiagramIcon from './DiagramIcon.astro';
// GitHub's gh-ost (2016 announcement post): how a trigger-based online schema change and a
// binary-log-based one both fill a "ghost" copy of a table. Top lane: triggers run inside every
// write. Bottom lane: gh-ost reads the binary log after commit and also copies old rows.
// Arrowheads are polygons: no SVG ids.

const W = 900;
const H = 430;

type Pt = [number, number];
// Polyline with an arrowhead at the last point; the line stops at the arrow's base.
function route(pts: Pt[], len = 10, half = 5) {
  const [x2, y2] = pts[pts.length - 1];
  const [x1, y1] = pts[pts.length - 2];
  const d = Math.hypot(x2 - x1, y2 - y1);
  const ux = (x2 - x1) / d;
  const uy = (y2 - y1) / d;
  const bx = x2 - ux * len;
  const by = y2 - uy * len;
  const line = [...pts.slice(0, -1), [bx, by]].map((p) => p.join(',')).join(' ');
  return { line, head: `${x2},${y2} ${bx - uy * half},${by + ux * half} ${bx + uy * half},${by - ux * half}` };
}

const iconFor = (en: string) => (en === 'App writes' ? 'laptop' : en === 'Binary log' ? 'log' : en === 'gh-ost' ? 'worker' : 'db') as 'laptop' | 'log' | 'worker' | 'db';
type Box = { x: number; y: number; w: number; en: string; vi: string; hot?: boolean };
const h = 54;
const top: Box[] = [
  { x: 20, y: 50, w: 150, en: 'App writes', vi: 'App ghi' },
  { x: 270, y: 50, w: 170, en: 'Original table', vi: 'Bảng gốc' },
  { x: 620, y: 50, w: 170, en: 'Ghost table', vi: 'Bảng ghost' },
];
const bottom: Box[] = [
  { x: 20, y: 214, w: 150, en: 'App writes', vi: 'App ghi' },
  { x: 215, y: 214, w: 150, en: 'Original table', vi: 'Bảng gốc' },
  { x: 410, y: 214, w: 120, en: 'Binary log', vi: 'Binary log' },
  { x: 575, y: 214, w: 110, en: 'gh-ost', vi: 'gh-ost', hot: true },
  { x: 730, y: 214, w: 150, en: 'Ghost table', vi: 'Bảng ghost' },
];

const routes: Pt[][] = [
  [[170, 77], [270, 77]],
  [[440, 77], [620, 77]],
  [[170, 241], [215, 241]],
  [[365, 241], [410, 241]],
  [[530, 241], [575, 241]],
  [[685, 241], [730, 241]],
  [[290, 268], [290, 318], [630, 318], [630, 268]],
].map((p) => p as Pt[]);
---
<figure class="dmgh">
  <div class="dmgh-scroll">
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Two ways to fill a ghost copy of a table during a schema change. Trigger-based tools: every write to the original table fires a trigger inside the same transaction that writes the ghost table, so triggers cannot be paused. gh-ost: writes land in the original table and the binary log; gh-ost reads the log after commit and also copies existing rows, then applies both to the ghost table, so it can pause at any moment.">
    <text x="20" y="28" class="dmgh-h">
      <tspan data-lang-en>Trigger-based tools (pt-online-schema-change)</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Công cụ dùng trigger (pt-online-schema-change)</tspan>
    </text>

    {top.map((b) => (
      <g class="dmgh-box">
        <rect x={b.x} y={b.y} width={b.w} height={h} rx="4" />
        <DiagramIcon name={iconFor(b.en)} x={b.x + 18} y={b.y + h / 2} size={18} />
        <text x={b.x + 18 + (b.w - 18) / 2 + 4} y={b.y + 32} text-anchor="middle" class="dmgh-name">
          <tspan data-lang-en>{b.en}</tspan>
          <tspan data-lang-vi>{b.vi}</tspan>
        </text>
      </g>
    ))}
    <text x="530" y="66" text-anchor="middle" class="dmgh-elabel">
      <tspan data-lang-en>trigger, same transaction</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>trigger, cùng transaction</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x="20" y="140" class="dmgh-bad">
      <tspan data-lang-en>Two tables fight for locks, and the triggers keep running when copying is paused.</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Hai bảng tranh nhau lock, và trigger vẫn chạy kể cả khi đã tạm dừng việc copy.</tspan>
    </text>

    <line x1="20" x2={W - 20} y1="174" y2="174" class="dmgh-rule" />

    <text x="20" y="202" class="dmgh-h">
      <tspan data-lang-en>gh-ost: reads the binary log instead</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>gh-ost: đọc binary log thay cho trigger</tspan>
    </text>
    {bottom.map((b) => (
      <g class={b.hot ? 'dmgh-box is-hot' : 'dmgh-box'}>
        <rect x={b.x} y={b.y} width={b.w} height={h} rx="4" />
        <DiagramIcon name={iconFor(b.en)} x={b.x + 18} y={b.y + h / 2} size={18} />
        <text x={b.x + 18 + (b.w - 18) / 2 + 4} y={b.y + 32} text-anchor="middle" class="dmgh-name">
          <tspan data-lang-en>{b.en}</tspan>
          <tspan data-lang-vi>{b.vi}</tspan>
        </text>
      </g>
    ))}

    {routes.map((p) => {
      const r = route(p);
      return (
        <g>
          <polyline points={r.line} class="dmgh-edge" fill="none" />
          <polygon points={r.head} class="dmgh-head" />
        </g>
      );
    })}

    <text x="460" y="338" text-anchor="middle" class="dmgh-elabel">
      <tspan data-lang-en>copies the existing rows in chunks</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>copy các dòng có sẵn theo từng đợt</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x="20" y="378" class="dmgh-good">
      <tspan data-lang-en>Writes are read from the log after they commit, so gh-ost can stop at any moment.</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Thay đổi được đọc từ log sau khi đã commit, nên gh-ost dừng được bất cứ lúc nào.</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x="20" y="402" class="dmgh-note">
      <tspan data-lang-en>The master sees one connection writing to the ghost table, in order.</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Master chỉ thấy một kết nối ghi tuần tự vào bảng ghost.</tspan>
    </text>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Both approaches build a copy of the table with the new schema and swap it in at the end. They differ in how they learn about writes that happen during the copy. Redrawn from the descriptions in GitHub's 2016 gh-ost announcement.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Cả hai cách đều dựng một bản sao của bảng với schema mới rồi hoán đổi vào cuối. Khác nhau ở chỗ biết về các lần ghi xảy ra trong lúc copy bằng cách nào. Vẽ lại theo phần mô tả trong bài giới thiệu gh-ost của GitHub năm 2016.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .dmgh {
    margin: 2em 0;
    width: 100%;
  }
  .dmgh-scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .dmgh svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 640px;
    height: auto;
  }
  .dmgh text {
    font-size: 14px;
    fill: var(--text-body);
  }
  .dmgh .dmgh-h {
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 700;
    fill: var(--text);
  }
  .dmgh-rule {
    stroke: var(--border);
  }
  .dmgh-edge {
    stroke: var(--text-muted);
    stroke-width: 1.4;
  }
  .dmgh-head {
    fill: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .dmgh .dmgh-elabel {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
    fill: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .dmgh-box rect {
    fill: var(--bg-alt);
    stroke: var(--text-faint);
  }
  .dmgh-box.is-hot rect {
    fill: var(--gold-tint-bg);
    stroke: var(--gold);
    stroke-width: 1.6;
  }
  .dmgh .dmgh-name {
    font-weight: 700;
    fill: var(--text);
  }
  .dmgh .dmgh-bad {
    fill: var(--red);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .dmgh .dmgh-good {
    fill: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .dmgh .dmgh-note {
    fill: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .dmgh figcaption {
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.55;
    text-align: center;
  }
</style>
